---
import { PRODUCT_MODELS, PRODUCT_MODEL_INFO, PLAN_LIMITS } from '@golem/shared';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE } from '../../lib/studio-plugin';
const free = PLAN_LIMITS.free;
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Apple and Apple MAX — Apple Docs"
  description="Choose Apple for limited free use or Apple MAX with an eligible paid subscription. Model choice is separate from permission to change your Studio place."
  heading="Apple and Apple MAX"
>
  <p>The selector beside the message box chooses a product model, not a planning mode.</p>
  {PRODUCT_MODELS.map(model => <section>
    <h2>{PRODUCT_MODEL_INFO[model].name}</h2>
    {/*
      THE STEP CEILING WAS NOWHERE A READER COULD FIND IT BEFORE SIGNING UP.
      A run on the free Apple lane is clamped to three steps — `maxStepsFor` in the worker takes the
      minimum of the mode's limit and Clay's — and /pricing sells the allowance in "quality-gated
      builds", a unit its own FAQ defines as read the tree, edit scripts, create instances, render,
      critique. That is five steps before the fix. The compute the page counts is genuinely
      delivered and the build genuinely completes, but it completes across several messages, and the
      only place that shape was ever stated was a "Step 2 of 3" counter during the run itself.
      Stated here and on the Free card; apps/site/tests/free-lane-steps.test.mjs reads the worker's
      own constant and fails when the two disagree.
    */}
    {model === 'apple'
      ? <p>Apple is the limited free model. It can answer questions and use building tools when Studio is connected and changes are allowed. It is not a read-only Plan mode. The Free plan includes {free.creditsPerDay} Credits per day, subject to its monthly allowance. A request has no artificial step or wall-clock ceiling: Apple keeps scheduling its own next step until the task is done, you stop it, access changes, or the account reaches its Credits/capacity limit.</p>
      : <p>Apple MAX is available to eligible paid subscribers. It uses the same measured strong foundation as Apple today, with paid entitlement, higher reasoning policy and MAX-only media/3D capabilities. It also runs without an artificial step or wall-clock ceiling. Choosing it on a free account shows an availability notice and keeps your draft; it does not switch your model or charge you. See <a href="/app/usage">Usage and plan availability</a>.</p>}
  </section>)}
  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>Paid checkout is not open in the current preview. Check <a href="/app/usage">Usage and plan availability</a> before expecting access to MAX. Extra purchased Credits do not by themselves grant a paid subscription.</p>
  <h2>What changes in Studio</h2>
  <p>Model access and edit permission are separate. Neither choice bypasses Studio pairing, change approval, quota, or tool safety checks. Without a connected plugin, a chat response is not a change to your place. {!STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE && <>Public plugin installation is currently unavailable. </>}See <a href="/docs/plugin">installation status</a>.</p>
  <h2>How Credits work</h2>
  <p>There is no guaranteed fixed charge per message. Actual usage and the plan limits determine the charge. See <a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits and limits</a>; review the result in Studio before treating a build as complete.</p>
  {/*
    THIS SENTENCE HAS NOW BEEN WRONG IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, so the history stays here.

      2026-08  "They currently share a foundation model."   true, then not.
      2026-09  "they run on different third-party foundation models"   true, then not.
      2026-09-21  same model again, and asked of the deployed Worker rather than read off a table:
                  one call per gateway key through /api/admin/model-test at buildSha 3236f91-dirty
                  returned @cf/zai-org/glm-5.3-flash for BOTH `stone` (every Apple request) and
                  `rune` (Apple MAX in Super Agent). Commit 8b61c91 then gave the two keys the same
                  6500 ceiling as well, so per single call the lanes are now identical.

    The guard beside this page was supposed to stop the second one going stale and did not, because
    it compared gateway key `clay` against `stone` — Plan against Agent — while calling that
    comparison Apple against Apple MAX. Apple is `stone` in every mode. It is re-aimed now and
    refuses whichever of the two sentences the gateway contradicts, rather than defending one.

    What the sentence is FOR has not changed through any of this: deny that either lane is a model
    we trained, and do not let a reader believe a paid lane buys a better brain per request. What it
    buys is steps and allowance, and that is what it now says.
  */}
  <h2>Training status</h2>
  <p>Apple and Apple MAX are separate product choices with different access and working limits. They currently run on the same third-party foundation model — neither is a model we trained — so what Apple MAX buys is a longer chain of steps in one request and a larger allowance, not a different or larger model. Custom Roblox training is in development; a completed independently trained frontier model is not available.</p>
</DocsLayout>
